WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.900
Good morning, John. I'm out for a hike with Catherine and Lemon.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.840
What's the difference between a hike and a walk? This is definitely harder than my average

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.700
walk

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.580
going uphill.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.780
I  want to make a couple of points in this video today.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.700
Neither of them have anything to do with what's going on around me

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.500
but hopefully, you will find that stuff interesting as well.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.840
We're out here hunting for wildflowers,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.680
and we're also looking for a geocache.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.399
Geocaching is fun.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.820
You know what geocaching reminds me of?

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.400
It reminds me of YouTube.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.640
A lot of cool people coming together and doing fun things and sometimes you know

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.980
troll comes in and spoils it for everybody.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.700
But most the time, there's just a lot of people who want to do something fun together.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.300
Geocaching, for those who don't know,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.860
is this little practice of hiding stuff and then leaving the GPS coordinates behind

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.160
and then people can come and find your cache

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.916
and they can add stuff to the cache and take stuff out of the cache

00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:41.040
and leave their name in the logbook.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:41.740
It's super fun.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.180
I was going to show you me finding the geocache,

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.100
but I can't find it,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.980
which is embarrassing.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.360
One of the two big points that I want to make in this video though, is that

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.820
YouTube is important.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.680
YouTube is important, interesting and fascinating on so many levels,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.660
and it's freaking awesome.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.580
But here's my real point.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.460
LOTS

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.580
of stuff is important.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.360
Mountains are important.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.460
Oxygen is important.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.900
PVC pipes are important.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.040
Motherboards are important.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.180
Motherhood is important.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.300
And all of these things are important.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.869
Saying that what you're doing is important

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:04.910
isn't unusual.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.420
The second thing that I want to add to this

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.120
is that important doesn't equal serious.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.840
I think personally fun is like the most important thing out there,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.880
except for trying to make the world a better place.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.900
Fun, man!

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.280
And I get so angry

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.500
when people start to make it about being serious

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.280
because you know what?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.220
Fun is important.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.620
Stephenie Meyer is important.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.300
Austin Powers is important.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.440
Weird Al Yankovic is important.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.120
And I don't care who hears me say it.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.279
John and nerdfighters,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.900
I think that we are all so lucky to be in new media,

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.800
where we don't have to take things so seriously.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.980
And the last thing I want, honestly, is for THIS to become serious business,

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.920
because then you start to lose the fun.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.640
FUUUUUUN.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:41.860
Ah!

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:42.900
Ahhh!

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.680
There's a log in that.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.160
Fun and beautiful.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.360
That's what I want for us.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.680
I cannot express

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.720
how lucky I feel

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:53.549
that I can go outside on a beautiful day, and share my thoughts with so many interesting and thoughtful people.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:54.520
So lucky

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.820
and I hope that we can distinguish between important

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:57.520
and serious

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.360
because to me,

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.209
serious has never even been on the agenda.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.620
What's on the agenda

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.460
is important

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.160
fun.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.480
This is important fun.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.500
Let's have it!

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.400
John, I will see you on Friday.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.280
We found it.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.940
[Whispering] We found it.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.400
Isn't that exciting?

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:13.920
Look!

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.020
Right there.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.660
This is the logbook.

